            <div xml:id="d695">

                <pb facs="0822" n="1656" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1656"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/609e</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-04T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 4, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6162. For McFadden [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 418. Repeat the following to Berne. We have advised Oederlin that we will postpone
                    discussion of the proposed extension of the Swiss agreement until the arrival of
                    Doctor Sulzer. Sulzer is expected here
                    momentarily. We will cable you further.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
